## 1. Lab Overview

This lab implements **Access Control Lists (ACLs)** on a Cisco router (`R Cafeteria`) using a Router-on-a-Stick (ROAS) inter-VLAN routing architecture. The goal is to enforce Layer 3 security policies that:

- Isolate guest network traffic (VLAN 30) from the management network (VLAN 10).
- Restrict remote administration access over SSH from the Point-of-Sale network (VLAN 20).

The lab also applies ACL placement best practices: **standard** ACLs close to the destination and **extended** ACLs close to the source.

