## 3. Configuration and Policy Application

### A. Standard ACL: Guest Isolation from VLAN 10

A named standard ACL was created to block traffic originating from the guest network (`192.168.30.0/24`) toward the management network, while permitting all other sources.

```text
enable
configure terminal
ip access-list standard BLOQUEAR_INVITADOS
 deny 192.168.30.0 0.0.0.255
 permit any
exit
```

**Application:** standard ACLs filter only by source IP address, so they are placed as close as possible to the **destination**: outbound (`out`) on the VLAN 10 subinterface.

```text
interface GigabitEthernet0/1.10
 ip access-group BLOQUEAR_INVITADOS out
exit
```

### B. Extended ACL: Remote Administration Restriction (SSH)

To limit remote administration access from the POS network (VLAN 20), a named extended ACL was configured to block TCP port `22` (SSH) originating from VLAN 20 toward any destination, while permitting all other traffic.

```text
ip access-list extended BLOQUEAR_ADMIN_REMOTA
 deny tcp 192.168.20.0 0.0.0.255 any eq 22
 permit ip any any
exit
```

**Application:** extended ACLs can filter by protocol, source, destination, and port, so they are placed as close as possible to the **source**: inbound (`in`) on the VLAN 20 subinterface.

```text
interface GigabitEthernet0/1.20
 ip access-group BLOQUEAR_ADMIN_REMOTA in
exit
```

### Placement Summary

| ACL | Type | Filters by | Interface | Direction |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: |
| `BLOQUEAR_INVITADOS` | Standard | Source IP | `Gi0/1.10` | `out` |
| `BLOQUEAR_ADMIN_REMOTA` | Extended | Protocol, source, destination, and port | `Gi0/1.20` | `in` |

