## 4. Verification and Test Results

| # | Test | Source | Destination | Expected Outcome | Result |
| :-: | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: |
| 1 | DHCP and 802.1Q trunk | Wi-Fi clients (VLAN 30) | Internet / `ISP` | Dynamic IP in `192.168.30.0/24` and Internet access | ✅ PASSED |
| 2 | Standard ACL | Wi-Fi client (VLAN 30) | Management network (VLAN 10) | `ping` fails with *Host unreachable* | ✅ PASSED |
| 3 | Extended ACL | VLAN 20 terminal | `ssh -l admin 192.168.10.1` | Connection rejected (*Connection timed out*) | ✅ PASSED |

**Test details:**

1. **DHCP and trunking:** correct 802.1Q tagging was validated on the switch trunk port, allowing VLAN 30 devices to obtain IP addresses dynamically and reach the Internet.
2. **Standard ACL:** a `ping` from a Wi-Fi client (VLAN 30) to the management network (VLAN 10) returns `Host unreachable`, confirming the ACL blocks the traffic.
3. **Extended ACL:** SSH connection attempts (`ssh -l admin 192.168.10.1`) from VLAN 20 terminals to the router are rejected (*Connection timed out*), enforcing the security policy.

### Router Verification Commands

```text
R_Cafeteria# show access-lists
R_Cafeteria# show ip interface GigabitEthernet0/1.10
R_Cafeteria# show ip interface GigabitEthernet0/1.20
```

- `show access-lists` lists each rule with its match counter (`matches`), which increments every time a test triggers the rule.
- `show ip interface <subinterface>` confirms which ACL is applied and in which direction (inbound or outbound access list).

